The U.S. Navy will conduct naval operations on October 13, 15, and 16, 2026, daily between the hours of 1200 and 1630. Operations will be centered along the coastline near the following positions: 
32.849482, -118.368963; 
32.852276, -118.372688; 
32.855606, -118.377128; and 
32.858666, -118.381018. 

All mariners are advised to remain well clear of the operational area and maintain a safe clearance of at least 4 nautical miles offshore of the southeastern coastline of San Clemente Island. On-scene safety and escort vessels will actively monitor VHF-FM Channel 16. For live range status or coordination, contact FACSFAC San Diego or hail San Clemente Range Operations on VHF-FM Channel 16.

A military training exercise will be conducted from October 5 through October 16, 2026, within the area bounded by the following coordinates: 

32.65295, -117.52161; 
32.67179, -117.32544; 
32.83719, -117.34778; and 
32.81850, -117.54384. 

Mariners are requested to maintain 1,000 yards of clearance from the operational area. For more details or comments, contact Cody Jorgenson at 218-260-1906. All mariners are advised to transit the area with caution.

The Scripps Institution of Oceanography research vessel SALLY RIDE (Call Sign WSAF) will conduct 24-hour surface-to-floor oceanographic operations from October 15 through October 18, 2026, within the area bounded by the following coordinates:

 33.356000, -118.390400; 
33.356000, -117.632000; 
32.523167, -117.632000; and 
32.523167, -118.390400. 

The exact timing and location of each station will depend on operational concerns and weather conditions. During over-the-side operations, R/V SALLY RIDE will be restricted in its ability to maneuver; all traffic is requested to give the vessel a wide berth. The vessel will monitor VHF-FM channels 16 and 13. For more information, contact the vessel master at sr-master@ucsd.edu or Heather Galiher at 858-226-8761. All mariners are advised to transit the area with caution.
